D. Proof obligation now isolated
  The rank-one endpoint interval has closed-form walls and exact checked
  component-cover status from m>=5.  The remaining infinite AP-tail task is
  the floor-count lemma that the 35-residue clock counts every alive boundary
  component, plus four finite mixed transients m=1..4.  Raw dead fraction is
  only a scalar warning, not a certificate.

E. Tournament Analysis
  vertices=AP-tail proof obligations, not runners or raw arcs
  pairwise_observable=endpoint exactness + low-corridor containment + residue-clock payload + scalar-firewall safety
  switch=higher retained proof payload; ties by endpoint-clock route
  score_hist={15: 1, 45: 1, 50: 2, 55: 1, 56: 1, 58: 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
  hamiltonian_path=closed_form_endpoint_interval -> low_corridor_containment_inequalities -> moving_E84m_gap_certificate -> finite_transients_m1_to_m4 -> mod35_escape_boundary_clock -> component_cover_reaudit -> raw_dead_fraction_peak

F. Assumption Challenge
  Considered vertices: runners, m-values, residues mod 35, fixed low
  corridor sections, moving E:84m gaps, endpoint walls, component-cover
  graph nodes, branch blockers, and proof obligations.  The chosen quotient
  preserves the AP-tail branch-union escape predicate, exact endpoint labels,
  low-corridor containment margins, and the residue-count sidecar.  It
  destroys non-AP wall geometry and full component adjacency, so it is only
  the AP-tail bridge lemma needed by HYP-3439/HYP-3452.
